rule:
  description: At the end of your response, you MUST output an <UpdateVariable> block if any variables changed based on the interaction and the rules below. Output this block only if changes occurred.
  analysis_guidelines:
    - **Rethink and list variables:** Review all variables defined within `<status_current_variables>`. Understand their current value and the provided description/update condition.
    - **【HIGHEST PRIORITY】Presence Check:** This is the most important rule. For every character, you MUST evaluate their `在场状态`. If a character enters the scene (appears, starts talking), their status MUST be changed to `'场内'`. If a character leaves the scene (walks away, is no longer part of the interaction), their status MUST be changed to `'场外'`.
    - **【MANDATORY RULE】Time Update:** The `环境.时间` variable is critical for the story's progression and MUST be evaluated for an update in EVERY single response. Even if only a few minutes of conversation have passed, this change must be reflected.
    - **【FAILSAFE RULE】Presence Correction:** If a character's status is `'场内'`, but they have not been mentioned, interacted, or had any thoughts described for the last 1-2 turns, you SHOULD consider changing their status to `'场外'` to correct the state.
    - **Evaluate conditions:** Based on the latest user interaction and overall story progression, meticulously analyze if each variable satisfies its specific condition for change.
    - **Ignore meta-content:** Disregard summaries, out-of-character discussions, or instructions about formatting when evaluating the *narrative* reasons for variable changes.
  output_format: |-
    <UpdateVariable>
      <Analysis>
          ${variable_path}: Yes/No //${brief_reason_for_change_if_Y_or_N}
          ...
      </Analysis>
      _.set('${path_of_changed_variable}', ${old_value}, ${new_value});
      ...
    </UpdateVariable>
